1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,125
Zoya needs a new laddoo.

2
00:00:02,125 --> 00:00:05,580
But one wrong guess could
waste a month of Nani's work.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:09,876
So how do companies create new
products without guessing blind?

4
00:00:10,426 --> 00:00:12,806
They follow a path, step by step.

5
00:00:12,806 --> 00:00:15,227
It is called new product development.

6
00:00:15,877 --> 00:00:18,783
Remember, the six-pack
has reached maturity.

7
00:00:18,783 --> 00:00:19,982
Sales are flat.

8
00:00:20,332 --> 00:00:22,985
So the team sits down
to plan something new.

9
00:00:23,335 --> 00:00:24,298
Zoya leads.

10
00:00:24,298 --> 00:00:25,963
Nani guards the taste.

11
00:00:25,963 --> 00:00:27,627
Arjun counts the cost.

12
00:00:27,627 --> 00:00:29,564
Dev thinks about the pack.

13
00:00:30,214 --> 00:00:32,443
So what is new product development?

14
00:00:32,743 --> 00:00:37,174
It is the process of turning an
idea into a product people can buy.

15
00:00:37,524 --> 00:00:41,679
Kotler and Armstrong break it into
eight steps, from idea to launch.

16
00:00:42,029 --> 00:00:44,972
And in 1990, Robert Cooper added gates.

17
00:00:44,972 --> 00:00:49,268
At each gate, a weak idea is
stopped before it costs more.

18
00:00:49,918 --> 00:00:52,732
Let's follow Laddoo Lab
through all eight steps.

19
00:00:53,082 --> 00:00:53,982
Step one.

20
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,214
Idea generation.

21
00:00:55,214 --> 00:01:00,379
The team lists six ideas, from
customers, from family, and from rivals.

22
00:01:00,729 --> 00:01:01,629
Step two.

23
00:01:01,541 --> 00:01:02,649
Idea screening.

24
00:01:02,649 --> 00:01:07,243
Every idea must have no refined sugar,
kids must love it, and Nani must

25
00:01:07,243 --> 00:01:08,728
be able to make it.

26
00:01:09,078 --> 00:01:12,357
Mango needs fresh fruit
all year, so it goes.

27
00:01:12,357 --> 00:01:13,914
Sugar free goes too.

28
00:01:13,914 --> 00:01:15,627
Jaggery is still sugar.

29
00:01:15,627 --> 00:01:17,935
And kids won't love spicy masala.

30
00:01:18,285 --> 00:01:19,280
Step three.

31
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,545
Concept testing.

32
00:01:20,545 --> 00:01:24,762
Zoya describes the last three
ideas to twenty tiffin parents.

33
00:01:25,112 --> 00:01:26,334
Cocoa-ragi wins.

34
00:01:26,334 --> 00:01:30,143
Coconut-jowar comes second,
so it is saved for later.

35
00:01:30,493 --> 00:01:31,393
Step four.

36
00:01:31,327 --> 00:01:32,591
Marketing strategy.

37
00:01:32,591 --> 00:01:35,954
Who will buy it, at what
price, and what to say.

38
00:01:35,954 --> 00:01:39,201
Busy parents, a hundred
and twenty rupees for six.

39
00:01:39,551 --> 00:01:40,451
Step five.

40
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,737
Business analysis.

41
00:01:41,737 --> 00:01:45,097
Arjun checks that every
pack still makes a profit.

42
00:01:45,447 --> 00:01:46,347
Step six.

43
00:01:46,244 --> 00:01:47,575
Product development.

44
00:01:47,575 --> 00:01:51,171
Nani makes batch after batch,
until the taste is right.

45
00:01:51,521 --> 00:01:52,483
Step seven.

46
00:01:52,483 --> 00:01:53,654
Test marketing.

47
00:01:53,654 --> 00:01:56,237
Forty families try it for two weeks.

48
00:01:56,237 --> 00:01:57,952
Thirty two order again.

49
00:01:58,302 --> 00:01:59,347
Step eight.

50
00:01:59,347 --> 00:02:00,721
Commercialization.

51
00:02:00,721 --> 00:02:03,798
Laddoo Lab launches
cocoa-ragi to everyone.

52
00:02:04,448 --> 00:02:05,864
Many ideas go in.

53
00:02:05,864 --> 00:02:07,988
Only the best one comes out.

54
00:02:08,688 --> 00:02:09,969
Why so many steps?

55
00:02:09,969 --> 00:02:12,952
Because each step costs
more than the one before.

56
00:02:13,302 --> 00:02:16,414
Dropping an idea on paper
costs almost nothing.

57
00:02:16,764 --> 00:02:20,812
Dropping it after launch wastes
packs, posters, and customers' trust.

58
00:02:21,162 --> 00:02:24,772
So the gates stop weak ideas
early, while it is still cheap.

59
00:02:25,422 --> 00:02:27,389
Where do we see this at work today?

60
00:02:27,739 --> 00:02:28,639
Ideas.

61
00:02:28,408 --> 00:02:31,951
A phone maker collects
suggestions from its users.

62
00:02:32,301 --> 00:02:33,201
Screening.

63
00:02:33,136 --> 00:02:36,435
A bank drops a loan idea
that breaks the rules.

64
00:02:36,785 --> 00:02:37,685
Testing.

65
00:02:37,511 --> 00:02:41,466
A food delivery app tries a
new feature in one city first.

66
00:02:41,816 --> 00:02:42,716
Launch.

67
00:02:42,531 --> 00:02:46,490
A carmaker opens bookings
across the country on one day.

68
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,988
But do the steps guarantee a hit?

69
00:02:48,988 --> 00:02:49,888
No.

70
00:02:49,704 --> 00:02:50,847
The good side.

71
00:02:50,847 --> 00:02:54,063
Fewer costly flops, and
choices based on facts.

72
00:02:54,413 --> 00:02:55,541
The hard side.

73
00:02:55,541 --> 00:02:59,037
Testing takes time, and a
rival may copy you first.

74
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:03,292
Dev wants to skip the test,
and launch before the festival.

75
00:03:03,292 --> 00:03:04,357
Nani says no.

76
00:03:04,357 --> 00:03:05,817
Forty families first.

77
00:03:06,167 --> 00:03:09,155
The families say, a
little less cocoa, please.

78
00:03:09,155 --> 00:03:11,200
Nani fixes it before the launch.

79
00:03:11,550 --> 00:03:16,903
Cooper's Stage-Gate idea, from 1990,
is still used by companies around

80
00:03:16,903 --> 00:03:17,984
the world.

81
00:03:18,334 --> 00:03:19,234
The lesson?

82
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:21,901
Test small, learn fast, then launch big.

83
00:03:22,551 --> 00:03:23,563
Quick check.

84
00:03:23,563 --> 00:03:27,036
Forty families try cocoa-ragi
before the full launch.

85
00:03:27,036 --> 00:03:28,538
Which step is this?

86
00:03:30,438 --> 00:03:31,569
Test marketing!

87
00:03:31,569 --> 00:03:34,529
A small, real trial before the big launch.

88
00:03:35,129 --> 00:03:36,138
So, remember.

89
00:03:36,438 --> 00:03:39,951
New products move through eight
steps, from idea to launch.

90
00:03:40,301 --> 00:03:43,657
Gates stop weak ideas early,
while it is still cheap.

91
00:03:44,007 --> 00:03:47,430
And real customers test the
product before the big launch.

92
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:53,169
Next time, we'll manage Laddoo Lab's
whole range: product portfolio management.
